  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rakesh Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 18 December, 2025 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Gwl:33719 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice G. S. Ahluwalia On The 18 th Of December, 2025 Miscellaneous Second Appeal No. 16 of 2024 Rakesh Kumar Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh And Others Appearance: Shri Prateek Kulshrestha - Advocate for appellant. Shri S.S. Kushwaha - Government Advocate for the State. Order 1.",
    "facts": "This miscellaneous second appeal under Section 71(6) of Food Safety and Standards Act has been filed against the order dated 19/9/2024 passed by Food Safety Appellate Tribunal/First District Judge Morena in MCA No.25/2024 as well as order dated 4/3/2024 passed by Adjudicating Authority/Additional District Magistrate Morena in case No.19/2022/Food Safety. 2. The facts necessary for disposal of present appeal in short are that on 13.02.2021 at about 3:15 pm, the Food Safety Officer carried out the inspection of Neha Kirana store and found that 15 kg of moong dal and 14 kg of besan were kept in a loose condition. Since the Food Safety Officer had suspicion about the quality of moong dal and besan, therefore, he collected the samples and sent it to the Food Analyst. The Food Analyst by his report informed that the moong dal was found to be of substandard quality. Accordingly, the report of the Food Analyst was sent to the appellant. He did not prefer an appeal under Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act and accordingly the complaint was filed. The appellant is a petty trader, and therefore, the penalty of Rs.1 lakh is on higher side. On 22/02/2024, counsel for the appellant expressed his inability to lead any defence evidence, and accordingly, the case was closed.",
    "arguments": "4. Challenging the order passed by the authorities below, it is submitted by counsel for the appellant that appellant was not given sufficient time to lead defence evidence.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Challenging the order passed by the authorities below, it is submitted by counsel for the appellant that appellant was not given sufficient time to lead defence evidence.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
